  "formula": {
    "tex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\term{pValue}{p}&=\\frac{\\min\\left(m\\,(\\term{larger}{M}+1),\\;\\term{permutations}{P}+1\\right)}{\\term{permutations}{P}+1},\n&\\term{larger}{M}&=\\min(\\term{greater}{g},\\term{lesser}{l})\\\\\n\\term{greater}{g}&=\\#\\{\\term{pairSum}{q_p}\\ge\\term{observedSum}{q_0}\\},\n&\\term{lesser}{l}&=\\#\\{\\term{pairSum}{q_p}\\le\\term{observedSum}{q_0}\\}\\\\\n\\term{observed}{s_0}&=\\term{scale}{\\kappa}\\,\\term{observedSum}{q_0},\n&\\term{zSimulated}{z}&=\\frac{\\term{observed}{s_0}-\\term{mean}{\\bar{s}}}{\\term{standardDeviation}{\\sigma_s}}\n\\end{aligned}",
    "ascii": "p = min(m (M + 1), P + 1) / (P + 1); g = #{p in 1..P : q_p >= q_0}, l = #{q_p <= q_0}, where q_0 is the pair sum of the identity permutation and q_p that of permutation p; the default two-sided tail has m = 2 and M = min(g, l) (greater: m = 1, M = g; lesser: m = 1, M = l; folded: m = 1, M = #{|s_p - mean| >= |s_0 - mean|}; directed: m = 1, M = min(g, l)). The statistic is s = kappa q with a positive constant kappa, so the counts compare identical f32 pair sums. z = (s_0 - mean) / sd of the P simulated statistics (esda z_sim). The p-value lies on the grid k/(P+1).",
